# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Claude Code local settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# Dependencies / build
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Third-party reference imagery (Brawl Stars / Zooba screenshots).
# Used locally as a quality bar for critics only — never redistributed.
reference/images/

# Generated renders and critic comparison sheets
shots/

# Original 2D prototypes — reference only, kept local and never published.
reference/prototypes/

# Uri's own device captures (screen recordings, phone screenshots). Local only.
# ⚠️ `reference/video/` was NOT covered when the first recording landed here, so a
# 4.9 MB capture of his phone sat committable for the length of one session. The rule
# in CLAUDE.md is about `reference/` as a whole, not about the two folders that happened
# to exist when it was written — so this ignores the directory, not a file pattern.
reference/video/
reference/videos/

# ── The blind-critic raw ledger — REFERENCE-DERIVED PROSE, NEVER COMMITTED ──────
# Every row carries a `referenceNote`: a critic's description of a third-party
# reference plate. `CLAUDE.md`'s security block says prose derived from viewing a
# plate is derived from it, and this repo is PUBLIC — that rule was breached once
# already by crop tables whose notes named a third-party character's costume.
#
# 🚨 THE FILE WAS UNTRACKED BUT NOT IGNORED, WHICH IS NOT THE SAME THING. One
# `git add tools/tmp` ships it, and agents pathspec-commit that directory
# constantly. A row was found on 2026-08-21 naming a third-party character
# verbatim; it was scrubbed in place, but the ACCIDENT PATH is what this line
# closes. `??` in git status distinguishes untracked from tracked — never safe
# from unsafe.
#
# ⚠️ Durability is handled instead by `tools/tmp/q1_public.mjs`, which commits a
# role-only projection: every score, floor and sha, and NO referenceNote text.
tools/tmp/q1_scores.jsonl

# ── AND ANY PARALLEL SCRATCH THAT FEEDS IT ────────────────────────────────────
# 🚨 A PATTERN THAT NAMES ONE FILE DOES NOT COVER THE DIRECTORY THAT FEEDS IT.
# `q1_scores.jsonl` was ignored on 2026-08-21 because every row carries a critic's
# prose description of a third-party reference plate. Running five panels in
# parallel then created `tools/tmp/q1_par/*.json` — five files, ALL FIVE carrying a
# raw `referenceNote` — untracked but NOT ignored, i.e. one `git add tools/tmp`
# from the same breach, in a PUBLIC repo.
#
# The ignore rule was written against a FILE. The exposure moved to a DIRECTORY the
# moment the work parallelised. Ignore the shape, not the instance.
tools/tmp/q1_par/

# ── AGENT ARTEFACT DIRECTORIES UNDER tools/tmp/ ───────────────────────────────
# 🚨 THESE HOLD RENDERED PIXELS, AND SOME FRAMES ARE COMPARISON SHEETS BUILT
# AGAINST REFERENCE PLATES. `reference/` itself is ignored; an output directory
# that CONTAINS a plate's pixels is the same disclosure by another route, and
# this repo is PUBLIC.
#
# Measured 2026-08-22 while closing the session: 63 untracked directories under
# tools/tmp/, at least 12 of them holding PNGs, one with 70. None was ignored.
# The TOOLS are committed — they are the instruments and the record of how a
# number was produced. The OUTPUT is not: it is regenerable by definition, and
# `shots/` was already ignored for exactly this reason while its siblings under
# tools/tmp/ were not.
#
# ⚠️ This is the THIRD time this session an ignore rule had to follow the work:
# q1_scores.jsonl (a file), q1_par/ (a directory), and now every agent scratch
# directory. Each time the reasoning was already written down and the shape of
# the work had moved. Ignore the SHAPE.
# ⚠️ AND THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS BLOCK ENUMERATED DIRECTORY NAMES — `*_out/`,
# `*_shots/`, `*_vs/`, and four literals. It left **31 of 63** directories
# uncovered, because agents name their scratch whatever they like (`gv_A20d/`,
# `ar2_shallow/`). Enumerating instances is what made the two earlier rules stale.
# The invariant is not the NAME, it is that a rendered pixel does not belong in a
# public repo: match the EXTENSION anywhere under tools/tmp/.
tools/tmp/**/*.png
tools/tmp/**/*.jpg
tools/tmp/**/*.jpeg
tools/tmp/**/*.webp
tools/tmp/**/*.gif
tools/tmp/**/*.log

# The extension rule above stops PIXELS leaking. It does not stop the rest of an
# artefact directory — run logs, per-station result JSON — from being swept in by a
# `git add tools/tmp`. Measured: 0 images but **309 paths** would still stage.
# An agent's OUTPUT directory is regenerable by definition; its TOOL is the record.
tools/tmp/*_out/
tools/tmp/*_out_*/
tools/tmp/*_shots/
